{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Charleston girl in a [B]darkened room
And [D]you don't know her [A]like I do
[E]We took the fire escape [B]to her room
And [D]got stoned, ragin' [A]blind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Left my money in the [B]trustin’ hands
Of them [D]ol' Steele Brothers in a [A]thrashgrass band
[E]One day I'm gonna [B]drive up there
and [D]give them half my [A]mind[A7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I don't know if it's the wine or the coke
That makes her sound like her jaw is broke
She's workin’ hard to make some sense,
but she ain't got a dime
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I wish to God that I could help her out
I wish I knew what she was talkin' 'bout
I wish to God that I could get away
but I'm way too drunk to drive
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[E]All I know is that when [Bm]I am good and sober
I am [D]leaving West Virginia for a [A]while
[E]Don't know why, but every [Bm]time I cross that river
Lord, there's [D]somethin' tears me up, makes me [A]wild
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Charleston girl with raven hair,
bloodshot eyes and skin so fair
I believe if I could find my keys,
I'd try to drive away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
I never planned to leave so soon
I didn't know that he was sweet on you
Go ahead and take her
'Cause she ain't worth the time
{end_of_verse}
